CORE
test.c
--nondet-volatile-write-model data:observe_data --nondet-volatile-write-model cmd:observe_cmd
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
data committed before GO: SUCCESS$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
--
Strongly-ordered device memory (the default, no --mmio-weak): the write models
are called in program order, so the write to the data register is observed
before the command and the ordering assertion holds. Same source as the weak
case, demonstrating that the reordering is what exposes the bug.
